1
00:00:00,845 --> 00:00:01,785
(Leonard:)Be mad at science.

2
00:00:01,946 --> 00:00:03,986
(Sheldon:)Don't you dare use
science against me.

3
00:00:04,949 --> 00:00:07,059
Science is my best friend!

4
00:00:07,218 --> 00:00:08,958
(Sheldon:)Oh, good,
I'm back up to eight.

5
00:00:10,321 --> 00:00:12,391
(Leonard:)Will you tell him
he's out of his mind.

6
00:00:12,557 --> 00:00:13,557
(Penny:)Actually, I get what he's saying.

7
00:00:13,725 --> 00:00:14,705
Yes! Nine!

8
00:00:14,792 --> 00:00:16,242
(Sheldon:)Welcome back, buddy.

9
00:00:18,530 --> 00:00:20,410
(Penny:)It's like if you're dating
someone you're not that into,

10
00:00:20,565 --> 00:00:21,665
(Penny:)and then they break up with you

11
00:00:21,833 --> 00:00:23,073
(Penny:)and then you want them
more than ever.

12
00:00:23,234 --> 00:00:24,734
(Sheldon:)I have no idea what
she's talking about.

13
00:00:24,903 --> 00:00:27,403
(Sheldon:)But we're ganging up on you
so I agree.

14
00:00:28,873 --> 00:00:30,913
(Leonard:)Okay, Sheldon, what do you
want me to do,

15
00:00:31,075 --> 00:00:32,245
(Leonard:)hide the information?

16
00:00:32,410 --> 00:00:33,980
(Leonard:)If I don't publish it,
it's just a matter of time

17
00:00:34,145 --> 00:00:35,145
(Leonard:)before someone else does.

18
00:00:35,313 --> 00:00:36,913
(Sheldon:)No, no, of course
you have to publish.

19
00:00:37,081 --> 00:00:38,861
(Sheldon:)That's your responsibility
as a scientist.

20
00:00:39,017 --> 00:00:40,517
(Sheldon:)Doing otherwise
would be unethical.

21
00:00:40,685 --> 00:00:41,755
(Sheldon:)You have no choice.

22
00:00:42,487 --> 00:00:43,557
(Leonard:)Fine, I'll publish.

23
00:00:43,721 --> 00:00:45,031
(Sheldon:)Can you believe this guy?

24
00:00:51,529 --> 00:00:53,369
Oh, Raj did the dishes.

25
00:00:53,531 --> 00:00:54,941
(Howard:)How do you know
I didn't do them?

26
00:00:55,099 --> 00:00:56,669
(Bernadette:)Because once,
when all the knives were dirty,

27
00:00:56,835 --> 00:01:01,025
(Bernadette:)you cut a bagel with your keys.

